# raon037-fix (commit e8bd14c08, this binary) measured arm (a) 122..126 tok/s on 387..512-token answers
# [measured]; a 2048-token answer reads deeper KV in the 7 latent layers, so the band opens 10 below
# [derived].
kind: baseline
question: what does one long Raon-1-mini-preview tape (Korean, n-predict 2048) show on one RTX 3090 at the
  serving defaults with the DFlash2 draft beside it?
term: decode tok/s of the K3 tape (Korean, about 50 prompt tokens, n-predict 2048), thinking as the template
  gives it, draft unset, RTX 3090, ctx 262144
unit: tok/s
predict: 112..130
condition: one lease, the box quiet, the 3090 alone, a fresh server, two discarded warm-ups, io pressure some
  avg10 under 5 before the tape, greedy
reason: the release post's Raon tape was too short; this is its long replacement
decide-in: publish it as the post's Raon tape
decide-below: under 112: the longer context costs more than raon037-fix's arm (a) shows; read the mtp width
  record before publishing
decide-above: beyond 130: the chooser opened on this prompt; read the mtp width record and the text
